    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d753">

                <pb facs="0854" n="568" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg568"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-03-06T20:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 6, 1916, 8 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3007. Your 3841 of February 23. Inform Foreign Office that porcelain guides for
                    Mitchell-Bissell Company requested on behalf of State Department should be given
                    immediate decision. Both in this <pb facs="0855" n="569" xml:id="pg569"/> and
                    cyanide application remind Foreign Office that Secretary of Commerce was assured
                    by English Ambassador that applications for goods necessary for American
                    industries would be granted. Delay is causing inestimable harm.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
